WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.801
-Our next guest
has his comedy special,

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:06.200
"Rage Against the Routine,"
available on YouTube.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.467
Making his late-night debut
here on "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.067
please welcome the very funny
Mike Feeney!

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:18.467
♪♪

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.501
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.300
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.067
Thank you so much, everybody.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.100
Wow.
I appreciate that.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.334
Exciting news --
I just celebrated seven years

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:29.868
of marriage with my wife.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.567
Yeah, yeah.
We've been married seven years.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.667
We'd been dating
a total of 17 years, though.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.501
Yeah, I know.
I had to make sure.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:40.934
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.968
If I'm being honest, she's one
of my favorite people right now.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.901
But when you're
in a relationship that long,

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.968
a lot of times, after shows,
from men, they'll come up to me

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.634
and they'll be like, "17 years."

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.601
I mean, my God,
I must have gotten so stale

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.434
in the bedroom by now, right?

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.868
And every time,
I have to explain to them, like,

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.734
"No, it hasn't gotten stale.
It's gotten efficient."

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.467
That's how I would --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.968
Yeah.
Like, our sex life is like

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.801
going to a Billy Joel concert
at this point.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.200
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.934
We're just playing the hits,
no new stuff, everybody's happy.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.100
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.968
Yeah.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.601
Yeah.
You're never gonna go

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.100
to a Billy Joel concert,
and he's gonna be like,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.100
"This is off my new --"
Like, "Buh buh buh! 'Piano Man,'

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.300
get to it right now.
Hurry."

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.767
"You know why we're here,
you know?"

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:25.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.601
My wife and I,
we got a dog recently,

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:29.934
which was such a great decision.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.968
'Cause we always had cats,
and I would defend cats.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.834
Any time someone
talked bad about cats, I'm like,

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.334
"That's 'cause
you never had one."

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.501
Once you get one, you realize
they got their own personality.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:39.334
They're cute, they're cuddly.
They're the best, you know?

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.267
And then we got this dog,
and I looked at the cats,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.033
and I'm like,
"I have never loved you.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.367
This relationship is over."

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:47.234
Like, I just --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.901
Because the doggy is adorable.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.801
He's, like, a 40-pound
lab-beagle mix.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:53.067
He's got the big dumb ears,
always looks like he's smiling.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.367
I love this little guy.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.734
But nobody told me
the social contract

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.033
that comes with having a dog.

00:01:58.033 --> 00:01:59.334
Very different from having cats.

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:00.634
I used to walk around
New York City.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:01.968
People don't really talk to you.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.734
Then you get a dog,
everybody wants to talk to you.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.200
But not about you,
about the dog.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.434
So, you have to learn
every single thing about them

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.434
because dog lovers
are crazy people.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.400
Did you know that?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.400
Dog lovers will just run up
to you with questions

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.634
that need answers right now.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:18.834
They're so aggressive.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.534
And for my dog,
it's always the same three.

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:21.868
They always go, "Oh, my God!
What's his name?

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:22.968
What kind of dog is it?

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.467
Is that as big
as he's gonna get? Oh!"

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:30.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.367
"Is that as big as he's gonna --

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.100
I'm gonna keep feeding him,
if that's what you're asking.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.934
What?
Yeah, he'll probably get

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.801
horizontally bigger
for the rest of his life.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.300
And then, God forbid,
you see another

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.767
dog owner with their dog.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.634
Now it's
a mandatory conversation.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.601
The second we see each other
down the block,

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.133
we have to start communicating
being like...

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.534
[ Laughing ]

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.234
"Yeah, yeah.
He's fr-- Can they say hi?

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.801
Okay!
Yeah, yeah, yeah!"

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:55.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.100
"Don't let the leashes
get tangled.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:01.167
Okay."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.901
And every dog owner will tell
you that their dog is friendly,

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.734
and almost none of them
are friendly.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:06.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.501
You don't even need
to look at the dog.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:09.767
The owner is like,
"No, he's good."

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:12.000
Like, they're getting yanked...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.834
...down the block while
the dog charges me like...

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.000
[ Imitating dog barking ]

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.133
Just full speed.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:19.501
And then stay start shouting
very specific commands at you.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:20.701
They're like,
"Let him get your scent,

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.300
but don't look at him
in the eye!"

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:24.734
It's like, "why?
What does that mean?

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:26.901
What'll happen?!"
You know?

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.300
"What's your dog's name?
Medusa? Oh, my God!"

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.067
Yeah.
I travel a lot for comedy.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.501
I have to fly often.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.434
I get very nervous
flying because -- fft! --

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:40.801
you know, that possibility.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:45.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.834
So, I drink on every flight
that I'm on.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.400
I don't care.
If it's 6:00 a.m.,

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.267
if it's 10:00 p.m.,
it's sky time.

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:52.934
You know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:55.434
The second that door locks,
I'm like, "I'll do a keg stand.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.400
Do we have one?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.934
I was flying across the country.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.200
It was an early flight,
and the woman came up to me.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.701
I was like, "Hi. Can I
please have a vodka soda?"

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:07.167
And the first thing she did
was she looked at her watch.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.334
I was like, "You can check
that judgment at the door.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:11.334
Okay?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:13.167
"Put that baggage
in the overhead compartment."

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.067
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.234
Yeah.

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:20.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. No way.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:24.000
Like, "You high-altitude hussy.
I will not be judged..."

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.234
"...by somebody who wears
a paper hat, you know?

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.567
Like..."

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.868
I didn't say that.
I'm a coward.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.701
I tried to make it easy for her.

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.534
So, I was like, "Oh, I'm gonna
have more than one drink.

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.367
Could I please open a tab?"

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.667
Which I thought was a very
normal sentence to say.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:40.868
And this was her reaction.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:44.400
She goes, "Sir, this is
an airplane, not a bar."

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.367
I'm not exaggerating
her shoulder.

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:50.033
She literally went,
"not a bar," like that.

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.567
She shimmied her shoulders
at me?

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:54.200
It made me furious.
I was like, "Oh, I'm sorry.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.801
I must've got confused
when you pushed

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:58.100
a mobile bar up to my seat..."

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:01.968
"...Frisbee'd a napkin at me..."

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.901
"...and said, 'What'll it be?'"
You know?

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.400
It's like, "You're a bartender."
You know?

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.467
"You're a bartender in the sky.
You're a sky tender.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.367
Call it whatever you want,
but --"

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:13.534
So, I got very petty.

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.167
I was gonna have two drinks
on the flight.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.133
Instead, I had six.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:19.601
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:21.133
And she did not
let me open the tab,

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.834
so I had to run my card
six times.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.234
And on the sixth time,
she came by with that

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:27.367
little credit-card machine,
and she was like, "Um, sir?

00:05:27.367 --> 00:05:29.167
I just want to let you know
there is, like,

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.367
a gratuity option on here.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:34.200
So, you know, in case
you want to leave a tip,"

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.767
and then handed it to me,
which made me so angry,

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:40.434
I had to return my seat to the
upright and locked position

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:41.834
and just looked her
right in the face,

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:42.934
I was like, "Oh, I'm sorry.

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:45.267
This is an airplane,
not a bar, so...

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:48.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:50.467
Thank you very much.
I'm Mike Feeney.

00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:52.167
♪♪

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.400
-That is how you do it, buddy!

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.467
Fantastic, buddy.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:58.467
That is how you do it
right there!

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:01.467
Mike Feeney!

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.300
"Rage Against the Routine"
is available on YouTube.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.300
We'll be right back, everybody.

